**Key Findings from Research Surrounding Movement to Work

* Participants need to clearly understand what support is available and how to make the best use of it
* Users need a simple and efficient way to find suitable work-experience and employment opportunities
* CV creation and improvement is a key area of support for people preparing for employment
* Work-experience opportunities are important for users who lack previous workplace experience
* Interview practice and preparation can help improve confidence before applying for roles
* Users may benefit from guidance on how AI can be used appropriately for job applications and interview preparation
* The benefits of completing the two-week programme should be clearly explained before users decide to take part
* Participants need help recognising the transferable skills they already have and understanding how to communicate them to employers
* The skills participants can develop during the programme should be clearly explained, including communication, teamwork, time management and digital skills
* Users should be able to easily understand what happens across the two-week programme before signing up
* The journey from initial interest through to programme completion should be broken into clear and easy-to-follow stages
* Local employers, sectors and available opportunities should be visible so users can understand what types of work may be available
* Travel distance, public transport availability and travel costs can affect whether an employment opportunity is realistic for a user
* Users may need support understanding job descriptions and identifying which skills are actually required for a role
* Participants should understand how completing the programme can strengthen their CV and provide useful experience to discuss in future applications and interviews
* Information should be presented using clear language and simple navigation so it is accessible to users with different levels of digital confidence
* Users should have a clear next step after completing the programme, such as applying for work, further training or accessing continued Jobcentre support
